WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.220
Speaker 1: All right. So the big media&nbsp;
story over the last 48 hours was Wednesday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:10.320
night's CNN town hall of the failed former&nbsp;
President Donald Trump. On yesterday's show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:16.380
we did an extensive review of what was&nbsp;
said. The audience's roll and reactions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:22.920
laughing and cheering at the most depraved,&nbsp;
anti-democratic and dishonest moments. Anchor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:30.600
Kaitlan Collins is respectable attempt to do some&nbsp;
fact checking up against the unfortunate reality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:38.520
that Trump mostly steamrolled right over her. Had&nbsp;
the crowd on his side for the lies and that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:47.100
environment in some total didn't really conform to&nbsp;
one where serious fact checking and pinning Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:52.020
down could happen in part because of the crowd and&nbsp;
because of the format and so many other things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.020 --> 00:01:00.300
So we then heard again on yesterday's show from&nbsp;
people in the media, Joe Scarborough and others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:06.000
members of the House and Senate. We heard from&nbsp;
all sorts of different people about the town&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.540
hall and we heard from voters as well. And in&nbsp;
a focus group that CNN did of Trump supporters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:19.620
they were not more impressed or less impressed by&nbsp;
Trump based on the town hall. It did nothing one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:24.000
way or the other to influence their opinion of&nbsp;
Trump. And then the question becomes, well, what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.920
about independent voters? What about Democrats?&nbsp;
What about non-Trump Republicans? And it's hard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.500
to imagine that they were overly thrilled by what&nbsp;
took place. So now there is a media question.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:42.480
What happens with CNN after this insane&nbsp;
town hall. We know that based on the new,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:48.360
relatively new leadership of CNN by Chris Licht,&nbsp;
that there is a change of direction happening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:52.560
that's already happened. The network has hired a&nbsp;
number of Republican former Republican officials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:59.340
and so on to to be on the network. But Chris Licht&nbsp;
did tell Kara Swisher during an interview back in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:05.640
November that CNN is not going to become the Trump&nbsp;
news Network. This was the current head of CNN,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:08.760
Chris Licht, speaking with Kara Swisher.
Speaker 2: You ended up talking about him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:11.820
for 8 hours a day. And we're not going&nbsp;
to do that. We're going to be very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:17.760
clear and take everything on a case&nbsp;
by case basis about what level of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:20.520
coverage it should be.
Speaker 3: So meaning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:24.780
that it will not be quite hand-waving.
Speaker 2: We are not going to be a 24&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:27.180
seven Trump news network.
Speaker 1: Okay.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:35.820
Is that what they are sticking to or is it not?&nbsp;
And to be clear, Trump is a former president&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:42.540
in the completely unprecedented situation where he&nbsp;
is under criminal indictment, was recently found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:50.820
liable civilly for sexual assault and defamation,&nbsp;
tried to hang on to power despite having lost. On&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:55.680
and on and on all these different things. So it&nbsp;
makes sense that corporate media talks about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:01.080
guy. It makes sense. But the question is, what is&nbsp;
the sort of tone and tenor of that coverage? Is it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:09.780
sycophantic? Is it what what exactly is it going&nbsp;
to be? Now, just as interestingly, in the 48 hours&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:18.240
since the Trump town hall, during which Chris&nbsp;
Licht defended what CNN did, there has been some,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:25.080
I guess we could call it lite rebellion coming&nbsp;
from within. Within CNN, There's an interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:34.140
article on Semaphore. America was served very well&nbsp;
by what we did last night. CNN chairman Defends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:45.240
Town Hall. But there are others who are quoted&nbsp;
here. The view from CNN staff is that it may not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:51.540
be particularly the best thing. And they point out&nbsp;
that they don't love the fact that the audience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:57.660
was filled with Trump supporters. CNN's senior&nbsp;
media reporter Oliver Darcy wrote, It's hard to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:02.880
see how America was served by the spectacle&nbsp;
of lies that aired on CNN Wednesday evening.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:10.560
And Licht said, I absolutely, unequivocally&nbsp;
believe America was served well. So there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:15.000
a couple of different questions here. Question&nbsp;
one is what actually happens on CNN as far as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:22.560
Trump coverage goes? Does it become friendlier&nbsp;
than maybe what we saw in 2016 and 2020? I don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:27.120
know. That's certainly one question. The other&nbsp;
aspect to this is what about disaffected Fox&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:31.680
News viewers? Because that's part of the timing&nbsp;
of this entire thing. Trump has increasingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:36.900
turned against Fox News over the last year. Now,&nbsp;
with the firing of Tucker Carlson, there is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:42.600
significant contingent of MAGA people who they may&nbsp;
be watching Fox News now reluctantly, or they may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:48.480
have abandoned Fox News and they want a new home.&nbsp;
Does Chris Licht want to appeal to those people?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:57.120
And does he want to try to make the new home&nbsp;
for those folks? CNN And can he do that in any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:01.800
way that is even remotely responsible as far as&nbsp;
journalism is concerned? Or can you really only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:07.320
appeal to those people by becoming overtly&nbsp;
sycophantic and brown nosing about Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:13.740
Trump? A lot of questions in this segment. Not a&nbsp;
ton of answers. We simply have to wait and see.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:19.020
But it's not looking particularly inspiring. I&nbsp;
think that's where we can leave it for today.

